natural_abilities:
  - { name: "Size and Life Span", description: "Average height 6 feet (1.8 m) and average weight 500 pounds before the species adjustment; the equipment entry gives 7 to 9 feet (2.1 to 2.7 m) as the usual size. 70% are male. Animal appearance with only a vague human, bipedal look: cat head, fur, tail, thick fingers with retractable claws; 85% have human legs, arms and build, and about a quarter run on all fours. Speech is partial and guttural, with hissing, growling and roaring when excited. Estimated life span 30-50 years. Running speed drops by 20% when climbing." }
  - { name: "S.D.C. and Armor Rating", description: "S.D.C. is the P.E. attribute number plus 1D6x10, plus those gained from physical skills and the species bonus. Natural Armor Rating 9+1D6: an attacker must roll above the A.R. to inflict hit point/S.D.C. damage; mega-damage weapons blast straight through an S.D.C. based A.R." }
  - { name: "Supernatural P.S. and P.E.", description: "33% of Kill Cats have supernatural P.S. and P.E.; the genetic improvement is available to African lions and tigers. With it, the bite does 1D6 M.D. and a claw attack 3D6 M.D. for lions or 4D6 M.D. for tigers." }
  - { name: "Sense Psychic and Magic Energy", description: "As the Dog Boy ability but less developed; constant and automatic, no I.S.P. cost. Base skill 30% +5% per level, rolled once every melee round; halved when several sources are scattered through the range. Range: 40 feet (12 m) +5 feet (1.5 m) per additional level to a psychic or mage NOT using powers; 300 feet (91 m) +20 feet (6 m) per level to psionic or magic powers in use. Roll every 400 feet (122 m) to stay on the trail; a failed roll loses the scent. Cannot Recognize Psychic Scent." }
  - { name: "Sense Supernatural Beings", description: "As the Dog Boy ability but less acute; automatic and constant, no I.S.P. cost. Base skill 54% +2% per level to identify the specific type of paranormal creature (alien intelligences, gods, demigods, demons, vampires, dragons) and to tell whether a person is possessed. Tracking by this scent: 10% +2% per level, or 23% +3% per level if the being is also using psionics or magic. Range 100 feet (30.5 m) per level to a being not using its powers; 1000 feet (305 m) +100 feet (30.5 m) per additional level when it is actively using supernatural powers, magic or psionics. Close proximity to ley lines and nexus points disrupts the sense." }
  - { name: "Psionics and I.S.P.", description: "Effectively a major psionic: saves vs psionic attack on a 12 or higher, with +2 to save vs psionic attack and all forms of mind control. Two powers of choice from the Sensitive category. I.S.P.: M.E. doubled, +2D6 per additional level. Recovers 2 I.S.P. per hour of activity or 8 per hour of meditation or sleep." }
  - { name: "Excellent Vision and Passive Night Sight", description: "20/20 color vision with a 220 degree field of view. The eyes amplify ambient light and see in darkness 6-7 times better than a human''s, but need some light (moon, stars, cloud glow). In total darkness the cat is blind, though smell, hearing and whiskers let it get about 2-3 times better than a human; blindness penalties are -4 to strike, parry and dodge." }
  - { name: "Excellent Hearing", description: "Registers sounds up to 25,000 vibrations per second (humans 20,000, dogs 35,000) and up to two octaves above the highest note a human hears; the ears prick and swivel, and tell apart two sounds five degrees apart with 75% accuracy. Judge distance and precise location of a sound''s source: 80% +2% per level. Recognize and identify prey (or a machine) by sound: 72% +2% per level, -20% for artificial sounds. Both lose 10% for every 50 yards/meters (about 150 ft / 45.7 m) between the cat and the source." }
  - { name: "Fair to Good Sense of Smell", description: "Most cats smell about twice as well as a human, nothing like a canine. A tiger relies on sight and hearing and smells no better than a human." }
  - { name: "Natural Climber and Swimmer", description: "All cats climb at a base of 60%/40% and swim at a base of 50% (tigers 86%), plus the species bonuses." }
  - { name: "Sprinter", description: "Can run at double normal speed for 1D4 minutes before dropping back to normal speed." }
  - { name: "Sensitivity to Ley Line Energy", description: "Ley lines and nexus points blot out the psychic and supernatural sensing abilities and give the cat a headache, so it cannot sense or track magic or supernatural prey there. Physical senses, sight especially, are unaffected and the other psychic powers are enhanced as usual. Cats are not vulnerable to ley line storms the way canines are." }
