side_effects: "Aggressive, dominant, self-oriented hunter-killers who love nothing more than to hunt and kill. About 50% of Kill Cats also suffer one or two of the Kill Hound''s aggression-based behavioral problems (Lone Star p.44-45): Extreme Aggression (fights over the slightest insult and cannot easily resist a challenge), Bloodlust (in a fighting frenzy forgets all orders and wants only to kill), Berserker Rage (a blind rage, oblivious to friend, foe and danger; one additional melee attack and +6 to damage while it lasts), Rage Syndrome (sudden irrational bouts of rage; one additional attack and +6 damage during the fit, then combat bonuses halved and one attack fewer for 1D6x10 minutes) or Jekyll and Hyde Syndrome (dramatic swings from pleasant to surly and looking for a fight). The Kill Hound list (printed 44-45) also has Ignore Pain and Sloth, which are left out here as not aggression-based. The problem shows less than in Kill Hounds because the cats work alone or in groups of 2-4 for long stretches in the wilderness; one who will not submit to a leader is forced out and usually ends up a lone hunter."
restrictions:
  - "R.C.C. Requirements: none, other than being relatively intelligent, loyal and obedient; all substandard creations are destroyed."
  - "The Mutation Abnormality Table and the other Optional Character Tables available to Dog Boys are NOT available to mutant cats. The Mutation Gone Wrong Table may be appropriate, pending G.M. approval."
  - "A player character who is not a CS agent must be a feral renegade (runaway or deserter) or the free-born offspring of runaway mutants; the CS terminates both on sight."
  - "Alignment: any, but 25% lean toward anarchist, 25% aberrant and 20% miscreant. Diabolic characters tend to be dedicated loners who do not work well in a group, even as its leader."
  - "Magic: none. Even feral and free-born Kill Cats avoid the study of magic, but may study magic weapons, charms and devices."
  - "Mutant felines in Coalition service are never taught to read."
  - "Cybernetics: generally none to start; about 10% have 1D4+1 bionic extras and 5% are partial conversion ''Borgs."
  - "Maximum rank: non-commissioned officer up to Sergeant Major."
  - "Pay: a token monthly salary of 30-60 credits, which accumulates in the bank for years. The entry prints no starting sum."
extraction_notes: "WB13 Lone Star printed 79-81 (cache p080-p082, cache page = printed folio + 1): the Kill Cats introduction and the R.C.C. heading are on 79, the stat block, skills, equipment and money on 80, and the entry ends on 81 where Monkey Boys begins. Numbers read off 170 dpi renders. The entry points to the Battle Cat (printed 76-79, cache p077-p080) for natural abilities, psionics, species bonuses and appearance, and to the Dog Boy for equipment; what it points to is restated here so the class stands alone and pairs with no race. || HEADING: a mutant-animal R.C.C. under Mutant Felines, a race. || XP: the ladder headed Dog Boy: Kill Hound, Feline: Kill Cat on the unnumbered Experience Tables page after printed 174 (cache p176; the render shows a folio of 175). || ATTRIBUTES as printed (Standard Kill Cat): I.Q. 3D6, M.E. 3D6, M.A. 3D6, P.S. 4D6+6, P.P. 4D6, P.E. 4D6, P.B. 3D6, Spd 4D6+6 running, reduced 20% when climbing (text). || POOLS: hit points P.E. x3 plus 2D6 per level. S.D.C. is printed as P.E. attribute number plus 1D6x10 plus those gained from physical skills: stored as sdc_base P.E. + 1d6x10, the same reading as the Battle Cat draft; each species ability states its printed extra S.D.C. in its own bonuses.pools.sdc. Because sdc_base is stated there is no men_of_arms line. P.P.E. 2D6. Armor Rating 9+1D6 is natural-ability text. Average weight is printed as 500 pounds (90 to 135 kg); the metric figure is the Battle Cat''s carried over by the book and is not stored. || SPECIES: the entry says bonuses and size vary by species as listed under the Battle Cat (printed 77, #5) and all bonuses are cumulative. Stored as a choice of one of six species abilities, each carrying its attribute, combat, save and pool bonuses; skill percentages, leaps, bite and claw damage are in each description. The book says Kill Cats are usually snow leopards, African lions and tigers, and elsewhere mentions leopard and puma Kill Cats; all six Battle Cat species are offered, lynx/bobcat included (judgement). Snow leopard is the leopard plus its printed extras (+1D6 H.P., +2D6 S.D.C., +1D6 P.S.), summed here to 4D6 H.P., 6D6 S.D.C. and 4D6 P.S. The lynx leap prints 15 feet (6 m) up; the metric is a misprint and only the feet are stored. Leopard prints +30 to climb with no percent sign; read as +30%. The tiger entry prints no S.D.C. bite or claw damage. 33% have supernatural P.S. and P.E. (M.D. bite and claw for lions and tigers): text. || PSIONICS (Same as Battle Cats, printed 77 #3-#4): major psionic, two Sensitive powers of choice, I.S.P. M.E. doubled plus 2D6 per additional level, +2 vs psionic attack and all forms of mind control (psionics 2, mind_control 2). || NATURAL ABILITIES: Battle Cat special abilities #1, #2 and #6-#12 restated from printed 76-78. || SKILLS: American at 90% is Language: Native Tongue 90, per_level 0. Basic Math is Mathematics: Basic 45. Radio: Basic 45+10 = 55. Climbing stored at the natural climber''s 60 in place of the catalog 40 (ability #9). Swimming 50 is not on the R.C.C. skill list; it is ability #10 (all cats swim at a base of 50%), stored as a skill so it appears on the sheet (judgement). Running. Prowl 25, no bonus printed. Intelligence 32+10 = 42. Escape Artist 30+10 = 40. Track Humanoids is Tracking (people) 25+10 = 35. Land Navigation 36+20 = 56. Wilderness Survival 30+20 = 50. Trap Construction 20+14 = 34 (the page prints +14%). Sniper. W.P. Knife (Vibro-Blade), W.P. Energy Rifle, one W.P. of choice. Hand to Hand: Martial Arts or Assassin as a choice of one; no price for another style is printed, so no hand_to_hand block. Species skill bonuses (prowl, climb, swim, acrobatics, tracking) are not added to any base; they are in the species descriptions. || RELATED: three, plus one at levels 3, 6, 9 and 12. Espionage +10, Mechanical Basic Mechanics and Automotive only, Medical First Aid only +5, Military +10, Pilot hovercraft, truck, sail and motorboat only +5 (Hover Craft (ground), Truck, Boat: Sail Type, Boat: Motor, Race & Hydrofoil), Rogue except Computer Hacking (no bonus, unlike the Battle Cat''s +5), Technical +10 except Computer Operation and Computer Programming, Wilderness +10; Electrical and Science none. Secondary: four, plus TWO at levels 2, 4, 8 and 11, same list without bonuses. Never taught to read is a restriction line; literacy skills are not excluded from Technical. || EQUIPMENT: the Kill Cat''s own basic list (printed 80). The armor is special DPM riot style armor of 70 M.D.C.; stored as the Dog Pack DPM riot armor row with the 70 M.D.C. in the note. Radio stored as the walkie-talkie row. 100 ft of rope as five 20 ft lengths. Two canteens. The list prints no firearm; rail guns and heavy weapons are made available, and Equipment Available Upon Assignment is not starting equipment, so none is stored. The printed comb is not stored: it has no catalog row and is a trivial personal item. || MONEY: a token monthly salary of 30-60 credits that accumulates in the bank for years. The Kill Cat entry (printed 80) prints no starting sum and never points to the Dog Boy pay rule, so no starting_money is stored; the salary is a restriction line. || Personality problems point to the Kill Hound list (printed 44-45): the entry says one or two of the same aggression based behavioral problems. Five are restated in side_effects; Ignore Pain and Sloth, also on that list, are left out as not aggression-based (judgement). Nothing is rolled. Identification coding, missions, numbers in service and the AWOL note are lore."
---

## Lore

Kill Cats are the heavy end of the Lone Star feline program: mutants grown
from the biggest hunting cats - snow leopards, African lions, tigers - and
bred for size, power and the same hard aggression the labs put into the Kill
Hounds. Fewer than six hundred are in service.

The Coalition does not garrison them. A Kill Cat is given a stretch of
wilderness as a hunting ground, shared loosely with a handful of others, and
one standing order: any nonhuman who enters and is not with the CS dies.
Against a group too large to take, the cat watches, weighs it up, and either
whittles it down over days of ambushes or shadows it and calls in a Dog Pack
or SAMAS flight. They are also sent after single named targets.

They live off the land for months, report by radio every two weeks and see a
base perhaps two or three times a year, which suits them. Most hunt alone;
lion-bred cats are the exception and gather in prides. They are reserved,
blunt and watchful like all mutant felines, and very few ever desert.

## GM Notes

Pick the species first: it sets most of the combat bonuses, the extra hit
points and S.D.C., and the size. S.D.C. is the P.E. attribute number plus 1D6x10 plus the
species dice. Roll the natural Armor Rating (9+1D6) once at creation.

The book prints no starting money, only a monthly salary of 30-60 credits.

The species percentages for prowl, climbing, swimming, acrobatics and tracking
are in the species text and are added by hand. One Kill Cat in three has
supernatural P.S. and P.E. (lions and tigers), which turns the bite and claws
into mega-damage attacks; decide that at creation.

Roughly half of all Kill Cats carry one or two of the Kill Hound''s aggression
problems. None of the Dog Boy optional tables apply to cats; the Mutation Gone
Wrong table is the GM''s call.

A Kill Cat that vanishes is presumed dead, and no hunt starts until someone
reliably reports it alive. One that stays far from Coalition territory is
unlikely ever to be found.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'kill-cat');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'kill-cat';

-- Records this run. REQUIRED: the smoke test fails a data script that has no
-- footer, or whose footer names a different file.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-kill-cat-class.sql');
